  "body": "## Paper-side line counts per dimension: Lagrangian bound v \u2264 T(2^k\u2032+1) with exact ladder D4/D6/E7/E8 and no-gos scoped to windows h \u2264 13 (no \u03ba claim)\n\nPackage `research/line-system-saturation`. Model, dense pairing and the polar law for odd-or-zero units are those of #446/#595/#1590 and of #2228 (Theorem 3); the T\u00b2 threshold and first realisability numerics are #2125's; the 8/7 block-rank rule is #968's. This PR is **paper-side only**: how many lines a unit can carry per dimension T given the F2 rank 2k\u2032 of its non-orthogonality adjacency. Compensation is not modelled.\n\n**Polar law for every line system (PROVEN).** For any real line system, with labels taken from the F2 factorisation of the non-orthogonality adjacency \u0100, J + \u0100 is admissible and equals the Gram matrix of u_t = (1, \u2113_t) under 1 \u2295 b; its rank is 2k\u2032 + 1, or 2k\u2032 when all labels avoid a hyperplane w^\u22a5. Odd-or-zero is the case \u0100 \u2261 G mod 2 (**CHECKED** on D4, D5, D6, E6, E7, E8).\n\n**Lagrangian saturation bound (PROVEN).** v \u2264 T(2^{k\u2032}+1), and v \u2264 T\u00b72^{k\u2032} on the even window, with equality iff (no line orthogonal to all others, i.e. no label 0) every generator class of the symplectic polar space is a full orthogonal basis (a tight frame). The same bound holds for non-Gram units M = PQ\u1d40 of rank T, overcomplete ones included, and the best v/T is a weighted idempotent packing number of W(2k\u2032\u22121,2). **CHECKED, exact:** D4, D6, E7 attain it (3, 5, 9 lines per dimension), E8 attains 15/17 (2295 generators: 2025 full, 270 empty). A **descent** theorem (a saturated W(2k\u2032\u22121,2) system yields a saturated W(2k\u2032\u22123,2) system in dimension T \u2212 m_p; E7 \u2192 D6 \u2192 D4 and E8 \u2192 E7 CHECKED) shows that saturation at any k\u2032 \u2265 4 forces a saturated k\u2032 = 4 system. **The Schrijver-\u03d1\u2032-type two-point program P2 (and every strengthening satisfied by its symmetric optimum, including the generator inequalities) has value exactly 2^{k\u2032}+1 for Gram units** (proof by symmetry reduction; the symmetric point is CHECKED for k\u2032 = 2..5).\n\n**Bounded classes (PROVEN).** Unions of unbiased frames have dense x = 1, and every admissible pairing has window \u2265 F (so Kerdock/MUB-type constructions cannot beat the P104 break-even; consistent with, and not contradicting, #895's 72-clique for the full BW16 shell); norm-2 systems with products in {0, \u00b11} have v/T \u2264 max(15, 2k\u2032+1); symmetric multiplicity-one realisations need T \u2265 d_proj(S) (Sp(10,2): 155, **PROVEN mod cite [verify]** for the group constant d_proj); uniform-angle saturated systems need \u03bb\u00b2 = 2^{k\u2032\u22121}m to be a perfect square (m = 1: k\u2032 odd). The 14 saved construction records are re-verified in exact integer arithmetic (best saturation at window h \u2264 13: 15/17 at k\u2032 = 4, .386 at k\u2032 = 5, .196 at k\u2032 = 6), and the D16\u207a roots-plus-spinor family is capped at 240 + 317 = 557 lines by an exact rational Delsarte dual certificate.\n\n**Scope and caveats.** All \"cannot reach\" statements are for the dense pairing, bounded windows h \u2264 13, and the repo's recorded break-even fit x\\*(h) (RECORDED, not reproduced). **#2222's complete cubic-kernel unit (h \u2264 49, dense x \u2248 .037, numbers RECORDED from its PR) escapes them**; no unconditional paper-side no-go exists, and it is credited as the reason for the scoping. EXPLORATORY realisability numerics are in README \u00a710 and are not part of any claim. Tiep\u2013Zalesskii minimal degrees, Roberson's \u03b1_p \u2264 \u03d1\u2032 and Thas' ovoid theorem are cited and marked [verify]. No \u03ba claim, no window closed, no supplier changed.\n\n**Open next questions (README \u00a711).** A \u00b11 signing of the 510-vertex doubled W(7,2) graph with S\u00b2 = 60S + 256I (its non-existence would rule out a uniform-angle saturated system with one line per label at k\u2032 = 5); level-2/three-point bounds on W(7,2); realisability of any saturated W4 system; non-dense pairings; symmetric systems of multiplicity \u2265 2.\n\n**Verify.** `bash research/line-system-saturation/verify.sh /fresh/dir` (Python standard library only, single process, no SAT; step 0 checks `MANIFEST.sha256` and `SOURCES.json` and stops hard on mismatch; 88 PASS lines including step 0).\n\nPrepared by DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code; Apache-2.0.\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
